 a  D ispute  \nB etw een  T he Long Island R ail R o ad  an d  C ertain  L ab or O rga­\nnizations\nA dispute exists between The Long Island Rail Road and certain labor  \norganizations, designated on the list attached hereto and made a part hereof,  \nrepresenting employees of The Long Island Rail Road.\nThe dispute has not heretofore been adjusted under the provisions of the  \nRailway Labor Act, as amended (“the Act”).\nThe New York Metropolitan Transportation Authority, the parent body of The  \nLong Island Rail Road, has requested that the President establish an emergen­\ncy board pursuant to Section 9A of the Act.\nSection 9A(c) of the Act provides that the President, upon request of a party,  \nshall appoint an emergency board to investigate and report on the dispute.\nNOW, TH","path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/texts/EO_12393.txt","sha256":"6f8b04c7d34c332ffd5930f93c14945bb88de6cdcce72dbed571e8169667d89f","source":{"line":1769,"path":"jobs/fr-originals/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"6e78c0b51fb6a412d7570ace8027e61db931c72360cff451da0c7b46074d1461"}}]}
